# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# /opt/start.sh boots LocalStack in the background (so the IAM resources are
# provisioned and awslocal can reach a LIVE endpoint) and then execs
# `sleep infinity` as PID-adjacent to the shell, so restarting/killing
# LocalStack cannot stop the container. Remediation is live AWS API calls, so
# there is no "forgot to restart" case.
